content.text:
Found it. In `vite.config.ts`, the build config has `sourcemap: false` — but the comment directly above it says the opposite of what it does:

```ts
build: {
    // Required for the Sentry plugin above to have anything to upload, and
    // for a production stack trace to resolve back to real source at all.
    sourcemap: false,
  },
```

That's the bug: with source maps disabled, minification (which Vite always applies in production builds) replaces function/variable names with single letters, and there's no map for Sentry (or you) to un-minify the stack trace with — even when `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN` is set, the plugin has nothing to upload. That matches exactly what you're seeing on the live site.

The fix is a one-line flip to `true`. It should also be `"hidden"` rather than `true` if you don't want the `.map` files to end up publicly served by whatever hosts `dist/` — but the Sentry plugin already deletes the maps after upload (`filesToDeleteAfterUpload`), so plain `true` is fine and matches what the surrounding comment already promises.

Want me to make that change (`sourcemap: false` → `true`) and sketch the PR per AGENTS.md's process, or do you want to confirm this is the intended fix first?

